namespace OpenTPW.UI.Original;

/// <summary>
/// Register of every UI value or rule that is not taken from original data or hard evidence
/// (docs/UI.md "Approximation register"). Each site carries a matching
/// <c>// [APPROX:UI-NNN]</c> comment; <see cref="LogOnce"/> reports them at startup.
/// </summary>
public static class UiApproximations
{
	public static readonly IReadOnlyList<(string Id, string Assumption, string EvidenceNeeded)> All = new[]
	{
		("UI-003", "the state selection of the original UI model draw beyond the stored selected-mesh endpoints is not traced; the instance traverser 0x57a530 composes each node's world matrix from its local matrix and its ancestors' (the root starts as its local matrix times the caller's, the identity set at 0x57a55b being overwritten), OpenTPW does the same, no ui.wad child carries a rotation or scale (only translations, which cancel in the selected-mesh fit), and the window angle (+0xe2) is ported as DrawFrame's turn (0x476c50)", "the UI control draw's selection of a state frame"),
		("UI-004", "UI model triangles drawn back to front by Z, grouped per texture; the original draws a UI model as nodes of the scene instance list: the walker 0x576910 (it sets global 0x8bb624 to 0x1000000 while it walks, which 0x581cd0 reads at 0x581cf6, 0x581cff and 0x581d15) appends their parts through the traverser 0x57a530 and 0x581cd0, and the frame batcher 0x581db0 gives every part its state word from its texture's alpha type (0x581790 -> 0x590c40, so a cut-out interface texture is tested at 0xf0/255 like a world texture), draws the states of bits 0x1000 and 0x2000 at once in file order with depth test and depth write on (decoder 0x567620 bits 0x8000 and 0x800 absent) and defers the others, far to near by the part's average depth (0x5829e0) with their triangles sorted by depth sum (0x565490); a part whose material word has bit 0x2 (state bit 0x800000, no shipped material) is keyed by its index span at 0x58109e instead; the display object's UI depth range is [0, 0.1) in front of [0.1, 0.2) and [0.2, 1) (defaults 0x582db4-0x582dc1), but how a UI vertex's depth reaches it (the transform at 0x87b1d8 +0xc) and whether the UI pass shares or clears the scene's depth buffer are not read, so the depth-tested file order is not ported", "the depth value the UI vertex transform (0x87b1d8 +0xc, called at 0x581092) gives a UI vertex, and whether the depth buffer is cleared between the scene and the UI nodes"),
		("UI-006", "text colours: window titles and the lobby island name yellow, the object windows' labels and values white, the pause menu's lines cyan (white while focused), green values elsewhere, grey disabled, the texture-switch progress bar track and backdrop colours (the video's 720p chroma is good to about +-15 per channel); the original gives each text control an RGBA colour (0x65c5d5 → renderer +0x48, kept as ARGB at +0x78, 0x48fd07; the sprite draw 0x58a010 takes it as the diffuse colour of the control's quads, 0x58a019) and renders its glyphs white (0x48fa96) unless the control keeps the font's own colours (+0xdd); the values traced are the options labels' (0,0,0,255) (0x4a441e), the buy list rows' (255,255,255,255) (0x4ad340), the pause menu lines' (0,175,190,255) (0x48b2b9) and the shared title colour (234,239,102,255) (0x492d20, fifteen window builders), with the lobby island name's second line (252,232,7,255) (0x4b8604) and a list row control that turns (140,0,60) on message 0x403 with a negative argument (0x4a0710); the other 0x65c5d5 calls (134 sites in all; by an instruction scan: about 36 with white (255,255,255,255), 31 with black (0,0,0,255) such as the runs 0x49ada6-0x49b385 and 0x4a53a2-0x4a5d26, 7 with red (255,0,0,255) at 0x49ff69, 0x4a002f, 0x4a6273 and 0x4b2e93-0x4b31f7, 5 with (224,86,86,255) at 0x4aa82d-0x4aac70, and about 45 that pass the colour from registers or tables) are not yet assigned to screens", "which screen each remaining 0x65c5d5 call colours (values, disabled states, costs) and the backdrop colours"),
		("UI-008", "text buttons without a UI model on purple_button art (ui.wad ships purple_button.wct, but no UI model of ui.wad names it and tp.exe holds no 'purple' string: the PC's labelled buttons are model-backed, b_login (button_text1, button_text2), b_dellog (b_pinkbutt, b_pinkbuttd), b_loantog (b_text, paybck, paybckd), and b_okay and b_exit through the dialog builder 0x47f020), so which art, if any, a PC screen gives a model-less text button is unread; each half is one end cap, drawn with its mirror image; upper half normal, lower half focused/pressed", "which PC screens draw a text button without a model and with which art (the name resolver 0x659bc9 and the UI model loader 0x488D20's state-to-texture mapping), or a capture of the original front-end buttons"),
		("UI-013", "the confirm dialog follows table 0x7583e8, the game-mode screen the name dialog 0x753f50 and the load screen the load dialog 0x7523f0, whose rows show the park's name and, right-aligned, the save file's local date and time as 0x49ec80 formats them (UITEXT 0x1c0 with day, month and year, then \" %02d:%02d\"; shipped parks and the sandbox have no file time and show none); the lobby's and the park's pause menus lay out their lines as 0x48c150 → 0x492f60 does (text width + 1 and height + 5 pixels on the canvas, centred, from top 10, 5 units apart), but the height follows OpenTPW's menu font tier ([EXT:ui-font-tier-by-scale]); the park pause menu's online variant is read and built (0x48c36c-0x48c4af: the first line at top 10 and each next 5 below the previous one's bottom, or top 0 and gap 0 while the net-session object's field +0x60, read by 0x5b6450, is non-zero; the field is cleared at creation (0x5b51a7), by every login reply other than 0x3c (0x5b6375-0x5b63dd, which store the status 0x4b, 0x4c, 0x4d, 0x4e or else 0x37 at +0x68), by the login teardown 0x5b6510 (0x5b6588) and by the other session resets (0x5b595f, 0x5b5e7d, 0x5b7a84, 0x5b7d6a, 0x5b7f0b); every store but one writes 0, and set to 1 only by the login reply 0x3c, 'ONLINE LOGIN: Authorization OK' (0x5b6303-0x5b6363, the handler 0x5b62e0 of the connect 0x5b5d10's reply callback 0x5b5ce0), so it is the original's logged-in state and OpenTPW maps it to the authenticated session the park HUD samples on opening (HudHost.IsLoggedIn); the measure 0x4929f0 is read and matched (it lays the text out in a box through 0x6ae1c0 and returns the block box, the widest line by lines times line height, which is OpenTPW's text layout box; with its wrap flag clear the box is 0x4000 wide, so nothing wraps); the focused line's hover ramp is built (0x48b2a0 sets the ramp slot to +1 on message 0x10001 and -1 on 0x10002, 0x48b220 steps it on every message 0x1e, eight frames at the 60 Hz reference, [EXT:frame-driven-at-60hz], from grey 0x21 in steps of 0x20 to white; the ramp is driven by OpenTPW's focus, [EXT:pause-menu-hover-focus])", "OpenTPW's menu font tier"),
		("UI-018", "the lobby draws the engine sky's cloud layer (sky.tga, coloured by the eased island colour) over the fog-coloured clear, without fog (the lobby's range 50 to 300 is set but the scene clears the fog enable, 0x5d8bf9; RenderFog, UI-107); while the globe is up the lobby's flyers and island clips keep stepping (the original's per-frame lobby update 0x5d5c50 has no globe branch and the main state stays 2, 0x54e6c7) but the island effects (lightning, thunder, rain, the nearest-island sky target) do not, where the islands component 0x5e0470 probably runs before the globe component sets the sky target and no rain each frame; whether the lobby scene is drawn then is not traced; the enter sequence is built (the camera turns to the island angle + π, the gate plays M1, the camera zooms under the black fade and the park starts below radius 8, 0x5e0490 states 1 and 2; an early leave's gate M2 close, 0x5e1350, is not reachable from the front end here); the key-unlock sequence is not traced", "the sky flags that enable the engine sky's draw (0x576a00), the registration order of the lobby's subsystems while the globe is up and whether the scene is drawn then, the key-award animation's code"),
		("UI-024", "the object windows (tables 0x755150, 0x755908, 0x755e80) draw their controls at the table rectangles and, for a shop or sideshow, the customer satisfaction gauge from the object's visit history (0x4e1e30), but the preview is OpenTPW's orthographic icon ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]); the local happiness gauge is 0x4cd880's mean over the 3 × 3 cells around the object's cell (every guest in the cell lists, the happiness float cut to a byte, the unsigned clamp of the high edge at 0x7f), as ported; the original takes the cell from the thing's own byte pair (+5, +7), which OpenTPW reads as the placement anchor, and its low edge wraps (x - 1 below 0 reads the last cell of the previous row, which is ported; y - 1 below 0 reads past the cell table, which no object reaches, since only owned land holds objects and the west and north fence lines are never owned); the build window fits the preview size to translated names and prices", "the thing cell byte pair (+5, +7) an object keeps and whether it is the placement anchor"),
		("UI-025", "the message tube admits ten occupied slots and refuses all new rows when full without eviction, sound or help (the tube's add routine 0x48EB20, the cap word 0x750610 = 10), and is saved with the park as an optional validated part of the resume save (the original's saver 0x48EE50, loader 0x48EF70); challenge progress refreshes tagged rows at capacity, while new progress/terminal rows refuse full occupancy; terminal instances survive reading/closing, expire unread after 30 unscaled seconds, and retain hidden slots for 500 ms after expiry/deletion; cross-tag replacement is synchronous; generic messages still leave on open; only offers carry actions and their original expiry/removal remains unwired; the tube art remains an extension", "original offer removal, full timer queue/focus/modal integration and other action-bearing sources; the original's own save record (OpenTPW writes its own JSON part and does not import an original save's tag block); visual validation and UI particles (PTCL-908)"),
		("UI-026", "build icons: the preview model (P<name>.MD2, else the main model) is drawn depth tested in its own image ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]) with the original's placement, camera and face test: the fit and footprint terms of 0x4689f0, the matrix 0x468e50 rebuilds each frame (the yaw and the -π/4 tilt through the sine table, the offsets, x scaled by 0.75 and depth by 0.1), the instance's own view diag(1, -1, 1, 1) (0x45bd30, 0x57a260, used for model flag 0x200 by 0x57a750), the viewport mapping with depth × 0.1 (0x579690 mode 2), the clockwise-only face test (0x581320) and LESSEQUAL depth (0x567620, 0x57360f), its turn of 0.0004 rad a millisecond running on across selections (0x46908a, 0x468e2f), and animation 5 started on each new preview (0x4732a0: <model>m1, else <model>m, looping); but the original lights the preview's vertices in its 3D object pipeline (0x57aa10) and OpenTPW draws them unlit; the selected item's footprint grid (8×8 cells coloured by cell type in control 0x1eb, 0x4ab1b0, record 0x754d50) is built (BuyFootprint), with the 1-pixel edges of its cell rectangles not traced; the object windows' previews keep a 30° tilt and 0.8 rad/s; sign faces use the object's rendered sign textures (ObjectSigns)", "the light set the 3D pipeline gives an instance drawn with its own view (0x57aa10 with the instance's second matrix slot +0x50, which 0x45bd30 does not write) and the pixel edges of the footprint cells"),
		("UI-031", "exactly Ctrl at the placing click keeps the build tool armed (0x5253b8; the Move tool's 0x5259e2), a ride with an entrance takes the queue tool after its placement whatever the modifier (0x52f580(3, 0)), and the queue tool's last click ends the tool whatever the modifier (0x5275b1..0x5275f2: 0x52f200(0, 0) sets mode 0 and replaces the build tool object, its mode 4 or 0x3b with its type, by the default tool), the tool's angle returning to 0 when it is left (0x52f3b6); the coaster tool ends the build tool at the placement whatever the modifier; the kart and water line tools (0xB, 0x10) take the queue tool when their circuit closes only while the placement's queue start 0x8186c0 is pending (0x526f95, 0x527004), from the cell the last placement stored (0x7639b8/0x7639bc), and the handover takes it (0x527056), as build and Move clicks on an accepted ghost (a click on a refused ghost returns at the latch first, 0x524a63), the Move pick-up and path or queue commits drop it (0x524b53, 0x5253f3, 0x525e5a, 0x527483), a path start cell ending the queue tool at once (0x52712f), and with no queue start exactly Ctrl keeps the line tool without a start (0x527146) and any other word ends it (0x527156); the Ctrl word 0xC at 0x5259e2/0x5259f4 is Ctrl alone (the modifier builder 0x46b420: Shift 3, Ctrl 0xC, Alt 0x30) and a placement that 0x52fab0 reports as entrance-bearing (the sub-record flag +0x40) takes the tail 0x5259ae: the queue re-evaluation 0x4de1f0, the words 0x763ac0 and 0x763ac4 back to 0x80, then the map cell record +0x29c (the cell's type word, +8 of the 0x44-byte record at +0x294) of the queue's start cell that 0x52a050 gave decides at 0x5259cf: type 1 (a path cell) ends the tool through 0x52f200(0, 0) whatever the modifier, which returns the angle to 0 as well (0x52f3b6); for any other start cell the mode stays the queue tool 3 that 0x52f580 set before, exactly Ctrl keeps the angle through it (0x525a06) and any other word runs 0x52f1b0(0, 0), which resets it (OpenTPW keeps the angle through the queue tool whatever the modifier and resets it when the queue tool ends); the coaster sub-mode (0x52faf0 = 3) takes the same tail and skips only the kart and water station line, so the tail itself enters the queue tool for a coaster as well, and the coaster's track tool (mode 0x15, 0x4474d0) is not entered anywhere in 0x524960; its click hands over to the queue tool when the pass 0x81 returns 0 (0x526525) only while a queue start is pending (0x52656e, taken at 0x526680), and otherwise ends the tool (0x5266bc), where OpenTPW's coaster tool enters the queue tool of a ride with one when the coaster is completed, pending start or not; which OpenTPW placements end at 0x5259cf is not mapped; Level.PlaceObject owns purchase/guest linkage and its removal handler owns scrap credits", "where the original's coaster placement enters its track tool, if it does (OpenTPW enters it at the placement; the callers of the tool builder 0x46c580 and of 0x4988c0 are not traced), what the coaster click's pass 0x81 returning 0 stands for, which of OpenTPW's placements have a path cell as the queue's start, and whether a tool armed while the queue tool runs (a buy-list item) keeps the angle exactly Ctrl kept at the placement (0x52f200 resets it only on its way to mode 0; OpenTPW starts that tool at 0)"),
		("UI-041", "Load Park takes no game type from the loaded park: the original derives GameType from flag bits 0x2000000/0x1000000 of 0x7a1a8c (0x550ca0), set by a front-end toggle (0x4bbf63), and the Mac saves none with a park", "whether a park file of the PC build can carry the game type (not traced)"),
		("UI-042", "the camera button's slide-out panel (table 0x751720) slides in and out as the arm drawer 0x4a14f0 does (ten 20 ms steps, cat_ui 0x1C and 0xC2, help 0x131): the drawer places the panel at the arm's left less the panel's own width and a horizontal gap of 50 (0x4a1631, the width read by 0x659e3e), centred vertically on the arm (the arm's top plus half the arm's height less half the panel's, 0x4a163b-0x4a1647) and then moves it right by a tenth of (the HUD window's right edge - the arm's left + the panel's width + 100) each step (0x4a16e5, the step 0x4a1704, the tick 0x4a19e7), the step being the integer quotient by the tick count 10 and the ten ticks adding it, so the panel ends at its start plus 10 times that step (the camera panel at left 482, top 1206; the message panel through the same drawer at left 486, top 1112) with the arm's art (bar, pane and handle) growing out from under the HUD; the camcorder button arms the C-key walk ([EXT:camcorder-first-person]) where the original's button 99 enters the camcorder at once (0x498ad0 → 0x481a10), and the walk's movement and look controls are not traced (the original's eye is terrain + 5 units, 0x42b1c0); the postcard window (table 0x7540d8) keeps its photo frame empty and its preview and address book buttons disabled (the 640×240 camcorder photo 0x4a9280, the preview redraw 0x4a84c0 and the address book 0x4a8140 are not ported); the original has no view-cycle button, so OpenTPW has none (0x751720 holds only the two buttons; no window control changes the zoom or yaw, and the locate jumps 0x42aab0 pass null zoom and yaw)", "the walk's key bindings (action table 0x787c14) and the time unit of its turn step; the photo, its preview and the address book"),
		("UI-047", "coaster HUD cost now distinguishes Build/Loop/Move tool mode 3 from other panel edits in mode 8; only an active height drag exposes mode-8 cost, matching 0x447990 and the 0x441A00 bit lifecycle. Cost arithmetic and spending are unchanged", "host panel selection still substitutes for the original mode-object stack, missing-panel fallback and the gate's mode type 4 are not qualified (no mode-object class returns 4: the vtables 0x6fe980-0x6fead0 return 7, 3, 1, 5, 6, 8 and 9); a button click during a height drag ends it without the commit where the original's 0x446fa0 calls the handler's second action 0x441a00 at 0x447032 (the cost is hidden afterwards either way)"),
		("UI-051", "the ticket counter is the player's earned tickets less the player's spent count (0x5af5d0, called by the HUD's counter handler 0x4a0fb0 at 0x4a10cd) while the park is part of its player's progress (the attached ledger, ParkEconomy.TicketWallet), and a ticket purchase adds its cost to the ledger's spent count and records the item in the player's bought set (0x4d4ad0 -> 0x5af740, 0x5af780), the park's older purchases entering the ledger once by identity; an Instant Action park spends from the same account and shows it (tp.exe skips the account only in game type 1, the online visit, 0x4d4ad0 at 0xfb3b7c), and a park outside the player's progress (the sandbox, a co-op session, a read-only visit) counts its own tickets and its own bought set; the key counter is the ledger's (0x5af680, matched)", "the sandbox has no player file to attach, and a park in a co-op session decides by the park's own records so that every peer decides alike ([EXT:online-coop-snapshot-join])"),
		("UI-060", "finance retains the eight series colours/order, selection masks, default bank balance, zero-inclusive scale, flat baseline, fractional series coordinates and hollow 3 x 3 pixel marks below 144 samples. Finance and park information share the opaque black backdrop, dark-green grid (0,100,0), green axes/step labels (0,200,0), plot (4,4,width-20,height-20), ten horizontal divisions and twelve labeled vertical spans for 12/36/144 samples (0x4806a0, 0x47fb50, 0x47fcd0); grid coordinates accumulate stored floats and truncate, primitive lengths are pixel counts, and the negative-minimum zero axis omits the bottom branch's extra pixel (0x47fc50). Empty histories and selections keep the backdrop. Signed 128-bit axis arithmetic for long financial values, background-only tiny/unsupported host controls and nonfinite-frame rejection are host safety adaptations", "original display-mode calibration of the retained two-canvas-unit pixel adapter; financial sample-to-month correspondence and stretching of available months; font, palette, raster and composited-output fidelity; a rendered composition of the graphs"),
		("UI-064", "the research knob now keeps raw0..1023, completed-click steps of one, press-relative saved-rectangle drags, release normalization, staffing refresh, workload cameo states and the clipped capacity gauge from static evidence; raw-zero startup retains the host-normalized bottom634", "whether native post-construction startup normalizes the authored ball top399 when the initial SetPos leaves raw0 unchanged"),
		("UI-082", "the hire figure now uses the traced inner rectangle, integer feet (626,362) and nominal 2.4 canvas units per reference pixel; native delayed FRAME/start/close/invalid-selection phase, global screen rotation, depth and exact viewport/raster parity remain qualified; the employed-tab figure deliberately shares the hire-box layout as EXT:staff-employee-view, not native applicant sourcing", "native scheduler and selection/close epoch parity, global rotation/depth and private real-data viewport/raster comparison"),
		("UI-086", "paths, queues and unowned land retain the native class 10..12 records; default live placed-object fills now read the exact current economy binding's Repair (PC object +0x44, SaveAttraction.StateOfRepair), round to stored float, truncate, mask the low byte and use the native integer 16.16 ramp (248,0,0 at 0; 248,200,0 at 50; 48,252,0 at 100; alpha 255, 0x5f09a0). Absent, read-only, mismatched or malformed state retains the old magenta fallback. Native cell-class/track priority, neighbour outlines, footprints and item dots remain incomplete; independent host excitement, thought and happiness overlays keep their existing precedence rather than native value-mode dispatch", "native value modes 2/3 (excitement 0x4e0860 and satisfaction 0x4e1e30), their controls and land modes (2444..2447, 2455..2457), exact cell-class/track priority (0x5f2050, 0x5f2fd0), open-status neighbour outlines/style 8 (0x5f2a94), item dots and footprints (0x5f44d0), and real-data/native rendered comparison; default repair semantics alone do not establish pixel equivalence"),
		("UI-091", "staff radios use independently persisted and validated role chains (+0x210), with explicit whole-role fallback for malformed original chains and read-only compatibility projection for older own saves; visitor radios project live guests onto the ThingPool used chain, with an explicit ascending-ID fallback only for pool-free fixtures; visitor position failure still clears the selection, while staff identity survives unavailable coordinates; camera follow lacks the original per-frame matrix blend of 0x42b1c0 (weight (1000 - dt) x 0.0005 of the previous frame, dt clamped to 1..1000 ms); panel sliding remains unimplemented", "camera smoothing and retained visitor position-loss behavior; slide geometry; exact-head C# validation and real-data visual comparison"),
		("UI-092", "the per-employee window uses ThingPool order, captured-target title rename and position-independent locator identity; its portrait observes current world output at yaw zero, with the existing role/variant elapsed hire-loop fallback when unavailable, and employee-only nominal 2.4 geometry at integer feet (526,476) from its inherited inner rectangle; control +0xE0 is UI depth, not animation phase", "independent-clone VM timing/state/flag history, native source-loss/refresh lifecycle, rotation/depth/occlusion and exact viewport/raster parity remain unimplemented or unverified"),
		("UI-094", "the ride view retains the camera-car/prototype eye and shared OriginalProjection; static now resets to 300 ms on an observed Boolean ride/terrain-eye edge, with positivity latched before elapsed-time subtraction (0x54faf7, 0x54fb20); host adaptations remain for single-sample monotonic timing, frame eligibility/initialization, the free-walk mapping, and the unchanged procedural noise", "native frame-gate/session lifecycle and mask bit 0x10; native noise sequence coupling and invisible window; seat/fallback axes and crowd target source; exact-head C# and real-data visual validation"),
		("UI-095", "leaving the ride view restores its prior camera instance, including the host terrain walk, and re-centres the host park camera on the object under its target with the original's test (0x42a340: a placed object whose type has CannotRide 0) and look direction (0x42a1d0: the link byte (+0xd) of the object's map cell, a 0x44-byte record at *0x7cf6ec + 0x294, masked with 0x55); the original's park camera is its own pose (yaw, height and smoothing in 0x42b1c0) that OpenTPW's host camera does not reproduce; the link byte is set whole by 0x5227e0 and cleared by bits by 0x5227f0 (called from 0x524960, 0x528a70, 0x52a050, 0x52a970, 0x52b400, 0x52ba50, 0x52fc80, 0x532fc0, 0x536490, 0x5367a0, 0x539670, 0x53af00, 0x53b280 and 0x53bb20; the writes of 0x524960 itself, at 0x524f1e, 0x5250ef and 0x525717, are on the second layer's cells of 0x28 bytes (the station line's flow link), never on an object's map cell) and reset by the cell reset 0x536490, and which of the other writers give a ride's cell its bits is not traced (OpenTPW's cell map keeps link bytes for path, queue and track cells only, so the yaw rule fires for none of the placed objects)", "which of the cell-link writers set the bits of a placed ride's cell, and the park camera's own pose"),
